ation alone.","difficulty":"extension","question_style":"conceptual","calculator":"neutral","estimated_time_seconds":75,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["graph interpretation","conceptual"],"choices":["f(−2)=0.","f(6)=0.","The minimum value is −9.","The y-intercept must be 0."],"correct_choices":["f(−2)=0.","f(6)=0.","The minimum value is −9."]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000058","syllabus_code":"SL 2.5","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"Data increase by approximately the same percentage in each time interval. Which model is most appropriate?","answer_data":{"answer":"Exponential"},"explanation":"A nearly constant multiplicative change indicates exponential behaviour.","difficulty":"foundation","question_style":"recall","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":35,"marks_estimate":1,"tags":["model selection","recall"],"choices":["Linear","Quadratic","Exponential","Inverse variation"],"correct_choices":["Exponential"]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000059","syllabus_code":"SL 2.5","type":"numeric_answer","prompt":"A taxi fare is modelled by C(d)=4.5+1.8d, where d is distance in km. Find the cost of a 12 km trip.","answer_data":{"answer":26.1,"tolerance":0},"explanation":"C(12)=4.5+1.8(12)=26.1.","difficulty":"standard","question_style":"application","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":60,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["linear models","interpretation","application"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":[26.1]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000060","syllabus_code":"SL 2.5","type":"matching","prompt":"Match each model feature to the most suitable family.","answer_data":{"pairs":[{"left":"Constant first differences","right":"Linear model"},{"left":"Constant second differences","right":"Quadratic model"},{"left":"Constant ratios","right":"Exponential model"}]},"explanation":"Differences and ratios help distinguish common model families.","difficulty":"extension","question_style":"conceptual","calculator":"neutral","estimated_time_seconds":75,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["model selection","data patterns","conceptual"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":[]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000061","syllabus_code":"SL 2.6","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"A height model is fitted using data for children aged 5 to 15. Which prediction is the least reliable?","answer_data":{"answer":"Height at age 35"},"explanation":"Age 35 is far outside the observed domain, so this is unsupported extrapolation.","difficulty":"foundation","question_style":"recall","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":35,"marks_estimate":1,"tags":["modelling","extrapolation","recall"],"choices":["Height at age 10","Height at age 12","Height at age 14","Height at age 35"],"correct_choices":["Height at age 35"]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000062","syllabus_code":"SL 2.6","type":"numeric_answer","prompt":"A linear model y=ax+b passes through (2,7) and (6,19). Find a.","answer_data":{"answer":3,"tolerance":0},"explanation":"a=(19−7)/(6−2)=3.","difficulty":"standard","question_style":"procedural","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":60,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["model parameters","procedural"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":[3]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000063","syllabus_code":"SL 2.6","type":"multi_select","prompt":"Select all questions that should be checked before accepting a model.","answer_data":{"answers":["Does its domain make sense in context?","Are the residuals reasonably small and pattern-free?","Does it predict impossible values?"]},"explanation":"Model quality depends on fit, domain and contextual reasonableness, not formula length.","difficulty":"extension","question_style":"conceptual","calculator":"neutral","estimated_time_seconds":75,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["model validation","residuals","conceptual"],"choices":["Does its domain make sense in context?","Are the residuals reasonably small and pattern-free?","Does it predict impossible values?","Does it have the longest formula?"],"correct_choices":["Does its domain make sense in context?","Are the residuals reasonably small and pattern-free?","Does it predict impossible values?"]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000064","syllabus_code":"AHL 2.7","type":"numeric_answer","prompt":"Let f(x)=x+4 and g(x)=x². Find (g∘f)(3).","answer_data":{"answer":49,"tolerance":0},"explanation":"f(3)=7, then g(7)=49.","difficulty":"foundation","question_style":"recall","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":35,"marks_estimate":1,"tags":["composite functions","recall"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":[49]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000065","syllabus_code":"AHL 2.7","type":"short_answer","prompt":"Find the inverse of f(x)=(x−1)/3.","answer_data":{"answer":"3x+1","acceptedAnswers":["3x+1","3x + 1"]},"explanation":"From y=(x−1)/3, swap x and y and solve: y=3x+1.","difficulty":"standard","question_style":"procedural","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":60,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["inverse functions","procedural"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":["3x+1"]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000066","syllabus_code":"AHL 2.7","type":"true_false","prompt":"For invertible f and g, (f∘g)⁻¹=g⁻¹∘f⁻¹.","answer_data":{"answer":true},"explanation":"Inverse operations undo the composition in reverse order.","difficulty":"extension","question_style":"conceptual","calculator":"neutral","estimated_time_seconds":75,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["inverse composition","conceptual"],"choices":["True","False"],"correct_choices":["True"]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000067","syllabus_code":"AHL 2.8","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"The graph y=f(x+3)−2 is obtained from y=f(x) by which translation?","answer_data":{"answer":"3 left and 2 down"},"explanation":"The inside +3 shifts left; −2 outside shifts down.","difficulty":"foundation","question_style":"recall","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":35,"marks_estimate":1,"tags":["graph transformations","recall"],"choices":["3 right and 2 up","3 left and 2 down","3 right and 2 down","2 left and 3 down"],"correct_choices":["3 left and 2 down"]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000068","syllabus_code":"AHL 2.8","type":"short_answer","prompt":"The point (4,−1) lies on y=f(x). Give its image on y=2f(x−3)+5.","answer_data":{"answer":"(7,3)","acceptedAnswers":["(7,3)","(7, 3)","7,3"]},"explanation":"The x-coordinate shifts right to 7 and the y-coordinate becomes 2(−1)+5=3.","difficulty":"standard","question_style":"procedural","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":60,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["graph transformations","coordinates","procedural"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":["(7,3)"]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000069","syllabus_code":"AHL 2.8","type":"multi_select","prompt":"For y=−f(2x)+4, select all true statements.","answer_data":{"answers":["There is a reflection in the x-axis.","There is a horizontal compression by factor 1/2.","There is a translation up 4."]},"explanation":"The coefficient inside f changes horizontal scale; the outside minus reflects outputs.","difficulty":"extension","question_style":"conceptual","calculator":"neutral","estimated_time_seconds":75,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["combined transformations","conceptual"],"choices":["There is a reflection in the x-axis.","There is a horizontal compression by factor 1/2.","There is a translation up 4.","There is a vertical stretch by factor 2."],"correct_choices":["There is a reflection in the x-axis.","There is a horizontal compression by factor 1/2.","There is a translation up 4."]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000070","syllabus_code":"AHL 2.9","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"A population approaches a limiting value as time increases. Which model is most appropriate?","answer_data":{"answer":"Logistic"},"explanation":"A logistic model levels off at its carrying capacity.","difficulty":"foundation","question_style":"recall","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":35,"marks_estimate":1,"tags":["logistic models","model selection","recall"],"choices":["Linear","Logistic","Quadratic","Direct variation"],"correct_choices":["Logistic"]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000071","syllabus_code":"AHL 2.9","type":"numeric_answer","prompt":"A radioactive sample follows M(t)=80(0.5)^(t/6). Find M after 18 hours.","answer_data":{"answer":10,"tolerance":0},"explanation":"After three half-lives, M=80(0.5)³=10.","difficulty":"standard","question_style":"application","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":60,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["half-life","exponential models","application"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":[10]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000072","syllabus_code":"AHL 2.9","type":"multi_select","prompt":"For L(t)=500/(1+9e^(−0.4t)), select all true statements.","answer_data":{"answers":["The carrying capacity is 500.","The initial value is 50.","The model is logistic."]},"explanation":"L(0)=500/(1+9)=50, and the horizontal limiting value is 500.","difficulty":"extension","question_style":"conceptual","calculator":"allowed","estimated_time_seconds":75,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["logistic models","parameters","conceptual"],"choices":["The carrying capacity is 500.","The initial value is 50.","The model is logistic.","The population grows without bound."],"correct_choices":["The carrying capacity is 500.","The initial value is 50.","The model is logistic."]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000073","syllabus_code":"AHL 2.10","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"If y=abˣ, which plot is linear?","answer_data":{"answer":"ln y against x"},"explanation":"Taking logarithms gives ln y=ln a+x ln b, a straight line.","difficulty":"foundation","question_style":"recall","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":35,"marks_estimate":1,"tags":["linearization","semi-log plots","recall"],"choices":["y against x²","ln y against x","y against ln x","1/y against x"],"correct_choices":["ln y against x"]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000074","syllabus_code":"AHL 2.10","type":"numeric_answer","prompt":"A plot of ln y against x has gradient 0.7. For y=abˣ, find b correct to three decimal places.","answer_data":{"answer":2.014,"tolerance":0.001},"explanation":"The gradient is ln b, so b=e^0.7≈2.014.","difficulty":"standard","question_style":"procedural","calculator":"allowed","estimated_time_seconds":60,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["linearization","parameter estimation","procedural"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":[2.014]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000075","syllabus_code":"AHL 2.10","type":"multi_select","prompt":"Select all true statements about a log-log plot of y=axᵏ.","answer_data":{"answers":["Its gradient is k.","Its vertical intercept is log a.","A straight line supports a power model."]},"explanation":"Taking logs gives log y=log a+k log x.","difficulty":"extension","question_style":"conceptual","calculator":"neutral","estimated_time_seconds":75,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["log-log plots","power models","conceptual"],"choices":["Its gradient is k.","Its vertical intercept is log a.","A straight line supports a power model.","Its gradient is always a."],"correct_choices":["Its gradient is k.","Its vertical intercept is log a.","A straight line supports a power model."]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000076","syllabus_code":"SL 3.1","type":"numeric_answer","prompt":"Find the distance between (1,2,3) and (4,6,3).","answer_data":{"answer":5,"tolerance":0},"explanation":"Distance=√[(4−1)²+(6−2)²+(3−3)²]=5.","difficulty":"foundation","question_style":"recall","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":35,"marks_estimate":1,"tags":["3D geometry","distance","recall"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":[5]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000077","syllabus_code":"SL 3.1","type":"short_answer","prompt":"Find the midpoint of (−2,4,6) and (8,0,−2).","answer_data":{"answer":"(3,2,2)","acceptedAnswers":["(3,2,2)","(3, 2, 2)","3,2,2"]},"explanation":"Average corresponding coordinates to get (3,2,2).","difficulty":"standard","question_style":"procedural","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":60,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["3D geometry","midpoint","procedural"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":["(3,2,2)"]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000078","syllabus_code":"SL 3.1","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"A closed cylinder has radius 3 cm and height 10 cm. Which expression gives its total surface area?","answer_data":{"answer":"78π"},"explanation":"Total surface area=2πr²+2πrh=18π+60π=78π.","difficulty":"extension","question_style":"application","calculator":"neutral","estimated_time_seconds":75,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["surface area","cylinder","application"],"choices":["30π","60π","78π","90π"],"correct_choices":["78π"]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000079","syllabus_code":"SL 3.2","type":"numeric_answer","prompt":"A right triangle has hypotenuse 13 cm and one leg 5 cm. Find the other leg.","answer_data":{"answer":12,"tolerance":0},"explanation":"By Pythagoras, the other leg is √(13²−5²)=12.","difficulty":"foundation","question_style":"recall","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":35,"marks_estimate":1,"tags":["Pythagoras","recall"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":[12]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000080","syllabus_code":"SL 3.2","type":"numeric_answer","prompt":"Two sides of a triangle are 8 cm and 11 cm with included angle 50°. Find its area in cm², correct to one decimal place.","answer_data":{"answer":33.7,"tolerance":0.1},"explanation":"Area=½(8)(11)sin50°≈33.7 cm².","difficulty":"standard","question_style":"procedural","calculator":"allowed","estimated_time_seconds":60,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["triangle area","procedural"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":[33.7]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000081","syllabus_code":"SL 3.2","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"A triangle has sides 7, 9 and 12. Which rule directly finds the angle opposite side 12?","answer_data":{"answer":"Cosine rule"},"explanation":"All three sides are known, so the cosine rule directly finds an angle.","difficulty":"extension","question_style":"conceptual","calculator":"neutral","estimated_time_seconds":75,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["cosine rule","method selection","conceptual"],"choices":["Sine rule","Cosine rule","Tangent ratio","Arc-length formula"],"correct_choices":["Cosine rule"]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000082","syllabus_code":"SL 3.3","type":"numeric_answer","prompt":"From a point 30 m from a tower, the angle of elevation to the top is 38°. Find the tower height, to one decimal place.","answer_data":{"answer":23.4,"tolerance":0.1},"explanation":"h=30tan38°≈23.4 m.","difficulty":"foundation","question_style":"application","calculator":"allowed","estimated_time_seconds":35,"marks_estimate":1,"tags":["angle of elevation","application"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":[23.4]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000083","syllabus_code":"SL 3.3","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"A ship travels on a bearing of 225°. In which general direction is it moving?","answer_data":{"answer":"South-west"},"explanation":"Bearings are measured clockwise from north; 225° points south-west.","difficulty":"standard","question_style":"procedural","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":60,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["bearings","procedural"],"choices":["North-east","South-east","South-west","North-west"],"correct_choices":["South-west"]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000084","syllabus_code":"SL 3.3","type":"true_false","prompt":"The angle of depression from a horizontal line equals the corresponding angle of elevation because the horizontals are parallel.","answer_data":{"answer":true},"explanation":"The two angles are alternate interior angles.","difficulty":"extension","question_style":"conceptual","calculator":"neutral","estimated_time_seconds":75,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["elevation","depression","conceptual"],"choices":["True","False"],"correct_choices":["True"]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000085","syllabus_code":"SL 3.4","type":"numeric_answer","prompt":"A circle has radius 9 cm. Find the arc length subtended by 80°, correct to two decimal places.","answer_data":{"answer":12.57,"tolerance":0.01},"explanation":"Arc length=(80/360)(2π·9)=4π≈12.57 cm.","difficulty":"foundation","question_style":"recall","calculator":"allowed","estimated_time_seconds":35,"marks_estimate":1,"tags":["arc length","degrees","recall"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":[12.57]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000086","syllabus_code":"SL 3.4","type":"numeric_answer","prompt":"A sector has radius 6 m and central angle 120°. Find its area as a coefficient of π.","answer_data":{"answer":12,"tolerance":0},"explanation":"Area=(120/360)π(6²)=12π, so the coefficient is 12.","difficulty":"standard","question_style":"procedural","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":60,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["sector area","degrees","procedural"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":[12]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000087","syllabus_code":"SL 3.4","type":"matching","prompt":"Match each central angle to its fraction of a full circle.","answer_data":{"pairs":[{"left":"90°","right":"1/4"},{"left":"120°","right":"1/3"},{"left":"225°","right":"5/8"}]},"explanation":"Divide each angle by 360°.","difficulty":"extension","question_style":"conceptual","calculator":"neutral","estimated_time_seconds":75,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["sectors","angle fractions","conceptual"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":[]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000088","syllabus_code":"SL 3.5","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"What is the gradient of the perpendicular bisector of the segment joining (0,0) and (4,2)?","answer_data":{"answer":"−2"},"explanation":"The segment gradient is 1/2, so the perpendicular gradient is −2.","difficulty":"foundation","question_style":"recall","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":35,"marks_estimate":1,"tags":["perpendicular bisectors","recall"],"choices":["2","1/2","−2","−1/2"],"correct_choices":["−2"]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000089","syllabus_code":"SL 3.5","type":"short_answer","prompt":"Find the equation of the perpendicular bisector of the segment from (0,0) to (6,0).","answer_data":{"answer":"x=3","acceptedAnswers":["x=3","x = 3"]},"explanation":"The midpoint is (3,0) and the segment is horizontal, so its perpendicular bisector is vertical.","difficulty":"standard","question_style":"procedural","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":60,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["perpendicular bisectors","equations","procedural"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":["x=3"]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000090","syllabus_code":"SL 3.5","type":"multi_select","prompt":"Point P lies on the perpendicular bisector of AB. Select all statements that must be true.","answer_data":{"answers":["PA=PB.","P is equidistant from A and B."]},"explanation":"The perpendicular bisector is the locus of points equidistant from the segment endpoints.","difficulty":"extension","question_style":"conceptual","calculator":"neutral","estimated_time_seconds":75,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["loci","perpendicular bisectors","conceptual"],"choices":["PA=PB.","P is the midpoint of AB.","P is equidistant from A and B.","∠APB=90° in every case."],"correct_choices":["PA=PB.","P is equidistant from A and B."]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000091","syllabus_code":"SL 3.6","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"Sites A=(0,0) and B=(8,0) share a Voronoi edge. Which point lies on their boundary?","answer_data":{"answer":"(4,3)"},"explanation":"The boundary is the perpendicular bisector x=4; every point on it is equally distant from A and B.","difficulty":"foundation","question_style":"recall","calculator":"not_