 simple graph has vertex degrees 2,2,3,3. How many edges does it have?","answer_data":{"answer":"5"},"explanation":"The degree sum is 10, which equals twice the number of edges.","difficulty":"foundation","question_style":"recall","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":35,"marks_estimate":1,"tags":["graph theory","degree","recall"],"choices":["4","5","8","10"],"correct_choices":["5"]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000116","syllabus_code":"AHL 3.14","type":"numeric_answer","prompt":"A connected graph has 8 vertices and 7 edges and contains no cycles. How many edges would its spanning tree have?","answer_data":{"answer":7,"tolerance":0},"explanation":"A tree with n vertices has n−1 edges, so 8 vertices require 7 edges.","difficulty":"standard","question_style":"procedural","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":60,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["trees","graph theory","procedural"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":[7]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000117","syllabus_code":"AHL 3.14","type":"multi_select","prompt":"Select all true statements about a complete graph K₅.","answer_data":{"answers":["Every pair of vertices is adjacent.","Each vertex has degree 4.","It has 10 edges."]},"explanation":"K₅ has 5·4/2=10 edges and contains many cycles, so it is not a tree.","difficulty":"extension","question_style":"conceptual","calculator":"neutral","estimated_time_seconds":75,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["complete graphs","degree","conceptual"],"choices":["Every pair of vertices is adjacent.","Each vertex has degree 4.","It has 10 edges.","It is a tree."],"correct_choices":["Every pair of vertices is adjacent.","Each vertex has degree 4.","It has 10 edges."]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000118","syllabus_code":"AHL 3.15","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"In an undirected simple graph, what does a 1 in position (i,j) of the adjacency matrix mean?","answer_data":{"answer":"Vertices i and j are adjacent"},"explanation":"Adjacency-matrix entries record whether the corresponding vertices share an edge.","difficulty":"foundation","question_style":"recall","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":35,"marks_estimate":1,"tags":["adjacency matrices","recall"],"choices":["Vertex i has degree 1","Vertices i and j are adjacent","There is exactly one vertex","The graph is complete"],"correct_choices":["Vertices i and j are adjacent"]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000119","syllabus_code":"AHL 3.15","type":"numeric_answer","prompt":"For adjacency matrix A, the entry (A²)₁₃ is 4. How many walks of length 2 go from vertex 1 to vertex 3?","answer_data":{"answer":4,"tolerance":0},"explanation":"The (i,j) entry of Aⁿ counts walks of length n from i to j.","difficulty":"standard","question_style":"procedural","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":60,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["matrix powers","walks","procedural"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":[4]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000120","syllabus_code":"AHL 3.15","type":"multi_select","prompt":"Select all properties of the adjacency matrix of a simple undirected graph.","answer_data":{"answers":["It is symmetric.","Its diagonal entries are zero.","The sum of row i is the degree of vertex i."]},"explanation":"Undirected adjacency is symmetric, and a simple graph has no loops on the diagonal.","difficulty":"extension","question_style":"conceptual","calculator":"neutral","estimated_time_seconds":75,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["adjacency matrices","graph properties","conceptual"],"choices":["It is symmetric.","Its diagonal entries are zero.","The sum of row i is the degree of vertex i.","Every entry must be 1."],"correct_choices":["It is symmetric.","Its diagonal entries are zero.","The sum of row i is the degree of vertex i."]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000121","syllabus_code":"AHL 3.16","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"Which algorithm constructs a minimum spanning tree by repeatedly adding th