ding variables.","answer_data":{"answer":true},"explanation":"Without controlled assignment, other variables may explain the observed association.","difficulty":"extension","question_style":"conceptual","calculator":"neutral","estimated_time_seconds":75,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["observational studies","confounding","conceptual"],"choices":["True","False"],"correct_choices":["True"]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000160","syllabus_code":"AHL 4.13","type":"multiple_choice","prompt":"A residual plot shows a clear curved pattern. What does this suggest?","answer_data":{"answer":"The chosen regression form is inadequate"},"explanation":"A systematic residual pattern indicates structure not captured by the model.","difficulty":"foundation","question_style":"recall","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":35,"marks_estimate":1,"tags":["residuals","model fit","recall"],"choices":["The chosen regression form is inadequate","The model is certainly perfect","All residuals are zero","The response variable is categorical"],"correct_choices":["The chosen regression form is inadequate"]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000161","syllabus_code":"AHL 4.13","type":"numeric_answer","prompt":"A model has total sum of squares 250 and residual sum of squares 40. Find R².","answer_data":{"answer":0.84,"tolerance":0.001},"explanation":"R²=1−40/250=0.84.","difficulty":"standard","question_style":"procedural","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":60,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["coefficient of determination","procedural"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":[0.84]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000162","syllabus_code":"AHL 4.13","type":"multi_select","prompt":"Select all signs of a useful regression model.","answer_data":{"answers":["Residuals are randomly scattered around zero.","R² is high for the modelling context.","Predictions are used within a reasonable domain."]},"explanation":"Same-sign residuals indicate systematic bias rather than a well-centred fit.","difficulty":"extension","question_style":"conceptual","calculator":"neutral","estimated_time_seconds":75,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["regression diagnostics","residuals","conceptual"],"choices":["Residuals are randomly scattered around zero.","R² is high for the modelling context.","Predictions are used within a reasonable domain.","Every residual has the same positive sign."],"correct_choices":["Residuals are randomly scattered around zero.","R² is high for the modelling context.","Predictions are used within a reasonable domain."]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000163","syllabus_code":"AHL 4.14","type":"numeric_answer","prompt":"If E(X)=12, find E(3X−5).","answer_data":{"answer":31,"tolerance":0},"explanation":"E(3X−5)=3E(X)−5=36−5=31.","difficulty":"foundation","question_style":"recall","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":35,"marks_estimate":1,"tags":["random variables","expectation","recall"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":[31]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000164","syllabus_code":"AHL 4.14","type":"numeric_answer","prompt":"If Var(X)=7, find Var(4X+2).","answer_data":{"answer":112,"tolerance":0},"explanation":"Var(4X+2)=4²Var(X)=16(7)=112.","difficulty":"standard","question_style":"procedural","calculator":"not_allowed","estimated_time_seconds":60,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["variance","linear transformations","procedural"],"choices":[],"correct_choices":[112]},{"seed_id":"51000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000165","syllabus_code":"AHL 4.14","type":"true_false","prompt":"Adding a constant c to every value of a random variable increases its variance by c.","answer_data":{"answer":false},"explanation":"A shift changes the mean but not the spread, so variance is unchanged.","difficulty":"extension","question_style":"misconception","calculator":"neutral","estimated_time_seconds":75,"marks_estimate":2,"tags":["variance","transformations","misconception"],"choices":["True","False"],"correct_choices":["False"